## The curves family: many curves in one structure of arrays, after Blender's
## CurvesGeometry and Houdini's curve primitives. Control points are f32
## positions over an f64 origin, like a mesh's points; `offsets` splits them
## into curves (curve c owns points offsets[c]..<offsets[c + 1]).
##
## Domains follow Houdini: the control points are the `point` domain and each
## curve is a primitive, the `face` domain, so group expressions, Group Type
## "Primitives" and attribute nodes address curves unchanged. How a curve is
## evaluated lives in builtin attributes, absent ones taking their default:
##
##   face   curve_type  int8     0 poly, 1 bezier, 2 NURBS, 3 Catmull-Rom (0)
##   face   cyclic      boolean  closed (false)
##   face   resolution  int32    evaluated points per segment or span (12)
##   face   order       int8     NURBS order, degree + 1, 2..8 (4)
##   face   knot_mode   int8     NURBS knots: 0 uniform, 1 endpoint, 2 custom (1)
##   point  w           float32  NURBS weight (1)
##   point  handle_l    float32x3 Bezier handles, in the positions' frame
##   point  handle_r    float32x3 (absent: automatic, Catmull-Rom tangents)
##
## Custom knots are one f32 column for every curve, split by `knot_offsets`.
## Evaluated positions, tangents, normals and lengths are a lazy cache
## (evaluate.lucb) keyed by the ids of the columns they read. A Curves is
## immutable once built; every operation makes a new one sharing what it
## did not change.
